speechtext:
Since the beginning of the war, how much was paid each year by the dominion government and any dominion board, commission and corporation and any other dominion agency to- 1. the law firm of Kearney and Duquet, barristers and solicitors, of the city of Montreal, and Kearney, Duquet and MacKay, barristers and solicitors, of the city of Montreal?
2. The following partners of the above mentioned firms:	(a) J. D. Kearney, K.C.;
(b) J. E. L. Duquet; (c) R. de W. MacKay; (d) W. Mitchell; (e) S. B. Ralston; (f) D. L. Gales?
